    {
      "family": "mrr_summation",
      "kind": "grid aggregation is not np.mean",
      "description": "The published grid mean aggregates rung MRRs with the builtin sum (metrics.py:479, :574), which CPython >= 3.12 computes with Neumaier compensation (proved on-box: sum([1e16, 1.0, -1e16]) == 1.0 while the naive loop gives 0.0). It differs from an np.mean-style (pairwise) replica in the last bit on 4/50 random 3-rung grids (<= 2.2e-16 relative). Per-rung metric values are bit-reproducible; the grid mean reproduces bit-for-bit only with the same builtin-sum implementation (CPython >= 3.12)."
    },
    {
      "family": "rounding",
      "kind": "deep-order noise at evaluation shape",
      "description": "At the evaluation shape (150x700, dim 200) the 5-dp payload rounding perturbs scores by up to ~1.4e-4, far above typical adjacent-score gaps (~1e-6) deep in a 700-item ranking: 446/450 rows have some order movement, 9/450 gold ranks move. MRR is largely insulated because it weights rank 1 only."
    }
